{
  "id": "29986_hanasu",
  "headword": "{放|はな}す",
  "reading": "はなす",
  "romaji": "hanasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to let go of; to release; to set free",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to let go of; to release; to set free",
      "explanation": "To stop holding something, or to let a captive creature go. The emphasis is on releasing one's grip or restraint, rather than on moving two things apart."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29986_hanasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "ロープを{放|はな}す。",
      "english": "Let go of the rope.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29986_hanasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{捕|つか}まえた{魚|さかな}を{川|かわ}に{放|はな}した。",
      "english": "I released the fish I had caught back into the river.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29986_hanasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}が{転|ころ}ばないように、{手|て}を{放|はな}さずにいた。",
      "english": "I kept from letting go of the child's hand so he would not fall.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive; the thing released is marked with を. The intransitive counterpart is {放|はな}れる (to come loose, to break away).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {手|て}を{放|はな}す: to let go with one's hand\n- {鳥|とり}を{放|はな}す: to set a bird free\n- {綱|つな}を{放|はな}す: to let go of the rope\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {離|はな}す: to separate; to move apart — same reading, but the focus is on creating distance between two things\n- {話|はな}す: to speak — an unrelated homophone",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
